---
description: Spring Boot Docker rules — reusable across Maven projects
globs: "Dockerfile*,docker-compose*.yml,Jenkinsfile,.dockerignore"
alwaysApply: true
---

# Scope

When asked to generate Docker files, create **only** at project root:

- `Dockerfile`
- `docker-compose.yml`
- `.dockerignore`

Do not add README or other files unless requested.

# Discover from project (never hardcode in rules)

Before writing, read the repo and derive:

| Value | Source |
|-------|--------|
| Java version | `pom.xml` → `<java.version>` |
| JAR name | `pom.xml` → `<artifactId>-*.jar` |
| App port | `application.properties` / `.yml` → `server.port` (default 8080) |
| DB type & name | datasource URL in config; include DB service in Compose only if project uses one |
| Image/service names | lowercase kebab-case from artifact or app name |
| Health URL | public GET endpoint (no auth) from controllers; fallback `/actuator/health` if actuator exists |

# Dockerfile

- Line 1: `# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1`
- Multi-stage: `builder` → `runtime`
- Base images: `eclipse-temurin:{java}-jdk-alpine` / `eclipse-temurin:{java}-jre-alpine`
- Use Maven wrapper (`mvnw`) when present; copy `pom.xml` + `dependency:go-offline` before `src/`
- Build: `./mvnw clean package -DskipTests -B`
- Runtime: install `curl`, non-root user `spring`, copy JAR as `/app/app.jar`
- `EXPOSE` discovered port; `ENTRYPOINT` (not CMD) with `-XX:+UseContainerSupport` and `-XX:MaxRAMPercentage=75.0`
- Short section comments (`# ---`)

# docker-compose.yml

- Services: `backend` + DB service (e.g. `mysql`) when project uses a database
- `restart: always`, bridge network `app-network`, named volume for DB data
- Backend: build from `.`, image `{app-name}:${BUILD_NUMBER:-latest}`, port `{port}:{port}`
- DB hostname in JDBC URL = Docker service name (e.g. `mysql`)
- Spring env vars override config: `SERVER_PORT`, `SPRING_DATASOURCE_*`, sensible JPA/logging defaults
- `depends_on` DB with `condition: service_healthy`
- Healthchecks: DB ping command; backend `curl -f http://localhost:{port}{health-path}`
- Header comment: app name + note to use `.env` if applicable

# .dockerignore

Grouped sections: build outputs, VCS/IDE, Maven (keep `mvnw`/`.mvn`, ignore `maven-wrapper.jar`), Docker/CI files, docs/env secrets, OS/logs, test artifacts.

Must exclude: `target/`, `.git/`, `.cursor/`, `Dockerfile*`, `docker-compose*.yml`, `.env`, `*.md`

# Jenkinsfile (when requested)

Create **only** `Jenkinsfile` at project root. Read `pom.xml`, application config, controllers, and existing `docker-compose.yml` first.

| Value | Source |
|-------|--------|
| `APP_URL` | `http://localhost:{port}{health-path}` from Discover table |
| Git branch | `main` unless user specifies |
| Git `credentialsId` | user prompt (e.g. `github-credentials`) |
| Git `url` | user prompt or `git remote get-url origin` |
| Maven build | `mvnw.cmd clean package -DskipTests -B` (Windows agent) |
| Failure logs | `docker compose logs backend` and `docker compose logs mysql` (match compose service names) |

**Pipeline:** declarative, `agent any`, `triggers { pollSCM('H/5 * * * *') }`, `environment { APP_URL = '...' }`.

**Stages (exact names, in order):** Git Checkout → Verify Tools → Build Spring Boot JAR → Docker Compose Deploy → Verify Deployment.

- **Git Checkout** — `git` step with branch, `credentialsId`, `url`; echo `Checkout source code`
- **Verify Tools** — `bat`: `git --version`, `java -version`, `docker --version`, `docker compose version`
- **Build Spring Boot JAR** — `bat 'mvnw.cmd clean package -DskipTests -B'`
- **Docker Compose Deploy** — `docker compose down` then `docker compose up -d --build`
- **Verify Deployment** — `ping 127.0.0.1 -n 25 > nul`, `docker ps`, PowerShell `Invoke-WebRequest` to `APP_URL` (exit 1 on failure)

Use `bat` for all shell steps (Windows Jenkins agent). No separate Test stage, no `docker push`, no `BUILD_NUMBER` image tag unless user asks.

**post success:** banner echoes + `Backend URL: http://localhost:{port}`

**post failure:** banner + `docker ps -a` + `docker compose logs` for backend and DB services

Do not add README or other files unless requested.

# Security

Use env vars for secrets. No production passwords in committed files.
